      "category": "Policy",
      "description": "Recommendation 1: For cesarean billing, require CPT 59510 when the \"same physician/group provides total care\" in the \"same global obstetrical period\"; reserve CPT 59514 for claims \"billed separate from global,\" with split billing if care is transferred or another physician delivers. Exempt: state or contractual exception, patient changes insurers, patient transfers practice, non-covering physician delivers. Peer: Cigna, Centene, and United Health all use 59510/59514 to separate global cesarean care from delivery-only cesarean billing..\n\nRecommendation 2: Limit CPT 59430 to \"59430 one time one unit\" / \"one postpartum package\" and allow it only for \"postpartum by another provider\" or \"59430 only if another provider\"; keep routine uncomplicated postpartum care included after the cesarean episode. Exempt: postpartum complications, problem-focused E/M after package. Peer: BCBS_KC, Cigna, and United Health all carve 59430 into a postpartum-only lane, with BCBS_KC and United Health limiting it to single-package use when another provider performs postpartum care..\n\nRecommendation 3: Bundle outpatient nondiagnostic services related to an inpatient cesarean admission when furnished \"three days prior to admission,\" \"one day prior to admission,\" or \"including day of admission\"; require modifier \"PD\" and enforce the \"3-day payment window\" / \"1-day payment window\". Exempt: critical access hospitals, RHC/FQHC all-inclusive rate, unrelated nondiagnostic services, ambulance services, maintenance renal dialysis services, SNF services, home health services, hospice services.",
